 ## 7. LRRP
 
+- A local user may ask an individual unit for one position from the contact actions. The request uses LRRP UDP 4001,
+  a four-byte transaction ID, and waits 12 seconds after transmit. An immediate report must match that ID, the station
+  ID and the channel key. A retune, unavailable TX, no fix and a missing reply are handled without keeping the remote
+  coordinates in the codeplug. Incoming reply settings are independent of the outgoing request.
 - Immediate location requests to us are answered; triggered requests (periodic, distance) start a trigger (2 at
   most, reports at most every 5 s) with a start response, then reports.
 - The position is the position service's ([position.md](position.md)), through the `ownPosition` hook the radio
diff --git a/docs/user/10-messages-and-signaling.md b/docs/user/10-messages-and-signaling.md
index a1909fe..234ea19 100644
--- a/docs/user/10-messages-and-signaling.md
+++ b/docs/user/10-messages-and-signaling.md
@@ -141,3 +141,8 @@ codeplug, so the [Codeplug Editor](04-programming.md) can set it too.
 
 LRRP answers location requests from a dispatcher. A radio without GPS ([Radio reference](23-radios.md)) answers "no
 fix". **Settings > Location > Answer GPS requests** turns the answers off.
+
+To ask a cooperating radio for one position, open a private contact's actions and choose **Position** on a
+conventional DMR channel that allows transmit. The result shows the coordinates reported by that radio, a response
+without a fix, or a timeout. Changing frequency, slot, or color code ends the request. Both radios need interoperable
+LRRP on UDP 4001. Replies are unauthenticated; use the action only with stations that agreed to share their location.
